WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.264
A paper receipt unfolds on a bright desk,
but its total has vanished.

00:00:05.264 --> 00:00:09.522
Beside it, a curve still shows how cost
changes with each unit.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:19.466
An arrow once pointed from total cost
toward marginal cost.

00:00:19.466 --> 00:00:24.426
It turns around now, asking which whole
function could have produced the rate

00:00:24.426 --> 00:00:25.189
we see.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:35.336
One possible cost curve rises into view.
Then another appears above it,

00:00:35.336 --> 00:00:39.632
following exactly the same slopes while
keeping a constant vertical gap

00:00:39.632 --> 00:00:40.022
everywhere.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:49.208
The gap becomes a movable block labelled
with a constant.

00:00:49.208 --> 00:00:53.477
Differentiation removes that block, so the
marginal curve cannot tell us its

00:00:53.477 --> 00:00:54.189
original height.

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:04.509
A single known cost value drops onto the
screen like an anchor.

00:01:04.509 --> 00:01:08.689
It selects one curve from the family and
fixes the previously missing level.

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:19.737
The receipt waits beside the marginal
curve and the possible totals.

00:01:19.737 --> 00:01:24.567
What information must we find before we
can recover one complete and reliable

00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:24.939
bill?
